course: dictionary
lesson: 4132
title: Glitch: a small fault
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A glitch is a small fault that stops something working properly, usually for a short time. You meet it most often with computers, games, apps and machines. «Game makers want glitches reported so they can fix them.» The sentence tells you what happens next: the makers find the fault and repair it.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «A glitch in a game may let a character walk through walls.» Walking through walls is not how a game should work, so a glitch is a fault that breaks the rules. Ask: what word would fit here? A small problem fits, but a planned feature does not.
explain: A glitch can also be a small, unexpected problem in a plan, such as a minor glitch on a school trip. Phrases like technical glitch and minor glitch show how big it is: usually small, and often easy to fix.
explain: Be careful with claims that sound too good. «A YouTube video promised a secret glitch for unlimited coins, 100% working». The comments say it works, but they come from accounts with no pictures and the same words. Those clues suggest the comments are fake. Using a glitch to win is unfair to others, so report it instead.
fact: A glitch is a small fault or problem that stops something working properly for a short time.
fact: Glitches happen most often in computers, games, apps, websites and machines.
fact: A technical glitch is a computer or machine problem; a minor glitch is a small one.
fact: Glitches come from rules in the code, so tell the makers exactly what you did.
fact: Using a glitch to win is unfair to other players, so report it to the makers.
exercise: «Game makers want glitches reported so they can fix them.» What will the makers probably do? | They will make the game longer | They will sell the glitches | *They will fix them | They will ignore them forever
exercise: «A glitch in a game may let a character walk through walls.» What is a glitch? | *A small fault that breaks the way something should work | A type of game character | A prize for winning | A fast new level
exercise: Dan says a glitch is a planned extra level. What does glitch really mean? | *A small fault or problem | A fast, shiny car | A kind of sweet | A planned extra level
test: The school trip had a small glitch when the bus was late, but the plan still worked. What does glitch mean here? | A big disaster | A rule for the bus driver | *A small, unexpected problem in a plan | A happy surprise
test: Ava found a glitch that let her win every match. What is the fair thing to do? | Share it with her friends so they can win too | *Report it to the game makers so they can fix it | Post it online with «100% working» on it | Use it all week to win more
exam: A video says «secret glitch for unlimited coins, 100% working», and the comments all look the same with no pictures. What should you think? | The video is from the game makers | The comments prove it must be true | Glitches always give free coins | *It may be fake, so check carefully before you trust it
